    "title": "Discourse Markers",
    "title_ko": "담화표지 (that said/having said that)",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Discourse markers manage the flow of an argument. 'That said' / 'Having said that' introduce a contrasting point after acknowledging something: 'The plan has risks. That said, I think it's worth trying.' 'All things considered' summarizes after weighing multiple factors.",
    "explanation_ko": "담화표지는 논지의 흐름을 관리합니다. 'That said' / 'Having said that'는 무언가를 인정한 후 대조되는 점을 소개합니다: 'The plan has risks. That said, I think it's worth trying.' 'All things considered'는 여러 요소를 따져본 후 요약할 때 씁니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "It was expensive. That said, it was worth it.",
        "ko": "비쌌어요. 그렇긴 해도 가치가 있었어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "Having said that, I still think we should try.",
        "ko": "그렇긴 하지만 저는 여전히 시도해봐야 한다고 생각해요."
      },
      {
        "en": "All things considered, it was a good decision.",
        "ko": "모든 걸 고려했을 때 좋은 결정이었어요."
      }
    ]
  },
